title    Midway Rush
composer Claude (ShooterCoaster)
about    Theme Park theme. Organ riff, accordion skank and an oom-pah tuba over a rock beat. Layers follow the combo: the organ riff, skank and tuba, then drums at 2x, the xylophone doubling at 3x, a supersaw and straight hats at FRENZY.
tempo    156
beats    4
steps    2
reverb   0.22

# untagged voices are the base layer, the riff among them (layers only add); the intro plays every layer
voice skank  accordion vol=0.35 pan=0.3  center=A4 gate=0.5
voice tuba   tuba      vol=0.8  oct=1
voice lead   organ     vol=0.75 pan=-0.1
voice hit    orchhit   vol=0.38 pan=0.1
voice kick   kick      vol=0.85          layer=drums
voice snare  snare     vol=0.55 pan=0.05 layer=drums
voice hat    hat       vol=0.35 pan=-0.3 layer=drums
voice crash  crash     vol=0.35 pan=0.2  layer=drums
voice timp   timpani   vol=0.5  pan=-0.15 layer=drums
voice xylo   xylophone vol=0.45 pan=0.35 layer=lead
voice saw    supersaw  vol=0.42          oct=1 layer=frenzy
voice fhat   hat909    vol=0.42 pan=0.4  layer=frenzy

pattern intro
xylo  | C5 D5 E5 F5 G5 A5 Bb5 C6 | .- C6- C6- .- |
kick  | x... x... | x... x.x. |
snare | .... .... | ..x. XXXX |

pattern A
lead  | C5 A4 C5 F5- E5 F5 A5 | G5- E5 C5- E5 G5 E5 | F5 D5 Bb4 D5 F5- Bb5- | A5 G5 F5 E5 G5--- |
skank | .- [F]- .- [F]- | .- [C]- .- [C]- | .- [Bb]- .- [Bb]- | .- [C]- .- [C7]- |
tuba  | F2- C2- F2- C2- | C2- G1- C2- G1- | Bb1- F2- Bb1- F2- | C2- G1- C2- E2- |
kick  | x... x... | % | % | x... x.xx |
snare | ..x. ..x. | % | % | ..x. .xXX |
hat   | .x.x .x.x | % | % | % |
crash | X... .... | _ | _ | _ |
saw   | C5 A4 C5 F5- E5 F5 A5 | G5- E5 C5- E5 G5 E5 | F5 D5 Bb4 D5 F5- Bb5- | A5 G5 F5 E5 G5--- |
fhat  | xoxo xoxo | % | % | xoxo xxXX |

# B keeps A's drums; the xylophone doubles the tune two octaves up
pattern B from A
lead  | D5- F5- A5- G5 F5 | F5- D5- Bb4--- | A4 C5 F5 A5 C6- A5- | G5 A5 G5 F5 E5- C5- |
xylo  | D6- F6- A6- G6 F6 | F6- D6- Bb5--- | A5 C6 F6 A6 C7- A6- | G6 A6 G6 F6 E6- C6- |
skank | .- [Dm]- .- [Dm]- | .- [Bb]- .- [Bb]- | .- [F]- .- [F]- | .- [C]- .- [C7]- |
tuba  | D2- A1- D2- A1- | Bb1- F2- Bb1- F2- | F2- C2- F2- A2- | C2- G1- C2- G1- |
saw   | D5- F5- A5- G5 F5 | F5- D5- Bb4--- | A4 C5 F5 A5 C6- A5- | G5 A5 G5 F5 E5- C5- |

play intro
loop A B

# Boss section (#598): the riff's minor twin, from the boss's arrival to its defeat: F minor, orchestra hits on the
# downbeats and timpani under the beat; the sting turns back to F major and the loop comes back.
